        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "one left at last; thus revolving day and night as if they",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "were two dice, the God of Death plays ( at dice ) with his",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "wife Kàli making mortals their dice-pieces and the earth",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "the board.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "44. With the setting and rising of the sun life becomes",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "shorter and shorter day by day; the lapse of time is not felt",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "in business which weighs down a man with the great weight",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "of work; the feeling of disgust is not awakened on beholding",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "the aggregate of birth, old age, misery and death; the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "world has been maddened by drinking the intoxicating wine",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "of delusion.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "45. Believing that the night is the same and again the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "same day, ignorant people run busily in the same manner",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "resolutely ( or secretly ) setting about their diverse vocations.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "Oh, how do we not, through infatuation, feel ashamed",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "( though ) disgraced by transactions in which there is a",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "repetition of the enjoyment of pleasures, and by this wordly",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "life of such nature !",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "46. For the annihilation of wordly existence we did",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "not contemplate the feet of the Lord, according to the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "prescribed rules; nor did we accumulate religious merit",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "which is capable of throwing open the doors of heaven; nor",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "did we embrace, even in a dream, the pair of the stout (full-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "grown) breasts and thighs of a beautiful woman. We have",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "been (serviceable ) simply as axes in cutting down the forest",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "in the form of our mother's prime of life.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "47. We did not in this world acquire learning capable of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "silencing a host of controversialists, and befitting modest",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "persons; we did not lead our fame to heaven by shattering",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "with the point of our sword the temples of elephants; we did",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "not, at moon-rise, sip the nectar of the tender-foliage-like",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "lower lip of our beloved; alas ! like a lamp in a tenantless",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "house, our youth has, indeed, passed away uselessly.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
